  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Power Africa:  Unlocking Southern Africa Solar (USAS) - Mega Solar</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">(USAID Africa Regional):  The Unlocking Southern Africa Solar (USAS) is a demand-driven program to facilitate the implementation of a large-scale solar competitive procurement program, under the Mega Solar initiative, in Namibia and Botswana. FY 2021 funds will:.Build awareness and consensus among development partners, regional institutions, and other stakeholders in Southern Africa for large-scale solar procurement programs focused on Solar PV and CSP technologies.Assess the technical and financial feasibility of large-scale solar programs in Southern Africa. Specifically, USAS will conduct technical, financial, and economic analyses to demonstrate the feasibility of large-scale solar procurements in Namibia and Botswana and the necessary steps for its launch. USAS relies on partnerships with governments and relevant regional stakeholders, such as SAPP, SADC, DFIs and Power Africa partners; and works with local development banks and power utilities to find innovative funding solutions for solar generation projects.Strengthen the institutional, technical and legal capacity in Namibia and Botswana to support their understanding of, buy-in for, planning, and implementation of a large-scale solar procurement program. Stakeholders such as the Ministry of Finance will need to understand the implications of various decision points in procurement design. Support coordination among existing Mega Solar partners and identify new partners, including local partners such as AUDA-NEPAD, to support Mega Solar priorities. USAS also increases the competitiveness of host-country entities in both Namibia and Botswana within the solar and renewable energy sectors through (i) facilitated access to donor finance, (ii) provision of necessary technical expertise, and (iii) coordination of the necessary platforms to achieve local and regional results..</narrative>
  </description>
